## Prisma Schema — Models

```
User          — id, name, username, email, password?, mobile?, avatar?, provider (local/google)
Workspace     — id, name, slug (unique), description?, logo?
Member        — userId + workspaceId (unique pair), role (OWNER/ADMIN/MEMBER)
Project       — workspaceId, name, slug, emoji?
Issue         — projectId, title, status (TODO/IN_PROGRESS/DONE), priority (Low/Medium/High),
                assignedTo (Member?), createdBy (Member?)
WorkspaceInvite — email, token (unique), role, expiresAt, accepted
GithubAccount   — userId (unique), accessToken, githubId, username
ProjectGithub   — projectId (unique), repoFullName, repoId, webhookId?
Activity      — workspaceId, actorId (Member?, onDelete: SetNull), action (enum), metadata JSON
Notification  — memberId (Member?, onDelete: SetNull), workspaceId, projectId?, title, message,
                type (enum), read (default false)
```

---

## Completed Features — Detailed

### 1. Authentication
- **Register** — Zod validation, OTP sent via Resend email, user created after OTP verify
- **Login** — email/password, bcrypt compare, JWT access + refresh tokens (httpOnly cookies)
- **Google OAuth** — Firebase popup, ID token verify backend, create/login user
- **JWT** — access token (15min), refresh token (7d), auto-refresh via Axios interceptor (queue-based, no duplicate refresh calls)
- **Logout** — cookie clear
- **Session restore** — `checkAuth()` Redux thunk on app load + login + register
- **Forgot Password** — email input → OTP to email → OTP + new password → reset (public route)
- **Change Password** — authenticated → OTP sent to registered email → same reset endpoint
- **Change Email** — OTP sent to new email → verify OTP → email updated
- **AuthGuard** — blocks logged-in users from /auth routes
- **PrivateGuard** — blocks unauthenticated users from / routes

### 2. Redis / OTP System
- **Layered architecture:**
  - `redis/client.ts` — ioredis connection singleton
  - `redis/core/cache.ts` — generic `setCache/getCache/deleteCache/updateCache` (TTL-aware)
  - `redis/otp/otp.service.ts` — domain-specific OTP logic built on generic cache layer
  - `redis/otp/otp.keys.ts` — centralized key naming (`otp:signup:email`, `otp:reset-password:email`, `otp:change-email:userId`)
- **Type-safe payloads:**
  - `BaseOtpPayload` (`otpHash`, `attempts`)
  - `SignUpOtpPayload` extends Base (name, email, username, passwordHash, mobile?)
  - `PasswordResetOtpPayload` extends Base (email)
  - `ChangeEmailOtpPayload` extends Base (userId, newEmail)
- **Generic `verifyOTP<T extends BaseOtpPayload>`** — attempts tracking (max 5), bcrypt compare, auto-delete on success/max-attempts
- **TTL: 300 seconds (5 min)** on all OTPs
- **Rate limiting** — OTP already sent check before resend

### 3. Workspace Management
- **CRUD** — create, read, update (name, description, logo via Cloudinary)
- **Slug generation** — auto-generated from name via `slugify`, unique constraint, P2002 handled with friendly message
- **Logo upload** — Cloudinary (multer middleware), old logo deleted on update
- **Cascade delete** — workspace delete cascades to members, projects, issues, activities, notifications, invites
- **Workspace switcher** — sidebar dropdown, `localStorage.setItem("lastWorkspace")` persisted

### 4. Invite System
- **Send invite** — email, role (ADMIN/MEMBER), 48hr expiry token (crypto), duplicate invite guard (excludes expired)
- **Email** — Resend with invite link
- **Validate token** — public endpoint, returns invite details
- **Accept invite** — verifies token, checks email match, creates Member, marks invite accepted, creates Activity + Notification
- **Invite page (`/invite/:token`)** — 3 cases handled:
  - Already logged in with correct account → accept directly
  - Logged in with wrong account → switch account option
  - Not logged in → redirect to register/login with token preserved in URL query param

### 5. Member Management
- **List members** — with user details
- **Remove member** — role-based permissions (OWNER can remove all, ADMIN can remove MEMBER only), FK constraint fix (`Activity.actorId onDelete: SetNull`, `Issue.assignedTo/createdBy onDelete: SetNull`, `Notification.memberId onDelete: SetNull`)
- **Change role** — only OWNER can change roles, OWNER role cannot be modified
- **Permission-based UI** — `useCurrentWorkspace` hook exposes `isOwner`, `isAdmin`, `isOwnerOrAdmin`, `isMember` booleans from cached workspace data (no extra API call)

### 6. Projects
- **CRUD** — create (OWNER/ADMIN only), read, update, delete (cascade to issues, activities, notifications, ProjectGithub)
- **Emoji picker** — project emoji/icon
- **Per-workspace** — scoped by workspaceSlug

### 7. Issues / Kanban Board
- **CRUD** — create, read, update, delete (OWNER/ADMIN only for delete)
- **Kanban** — drag-and-drop via `@dnd-kit/core` (`DndContext`, `useDraggable`/`useDroppable`)
- **Columns** — TODO / IN_PROGRESS / DONE
- **Priority** — Low / Medium / High
- **Assignee** — from workspace members
- **Status update** — drag triggers `PATCH` API
- **Reusable `IssueForm`** — same component for create + edit via `defaultValues` + `submitLabel` props
- **Sheet-based edit** — `UpdateIssue.tsx` uses shadcn Sheet
- **"My Issues"** — dashboard widget showing issues assigned to current user

### 8. GitHub Integration
- **OAuth App** — Client ID/Secret stored in `.env`
- **Connect flow** — `/github/:workspaceSlug/connect` → GitHub auth URL (JWT-signed `state`) → callback → exchange code for token → store in `GithubAccount`
- **Repo listing** — fetch user repos from GitHub API
- **Link repo to project** — creates `ProjectGithub`, registers webhook on GitHub via API
- **Unlink repo** — deletes webhook from GitHub + `ProjectGithub` record
- **Unlink account** — deletes `GithubAccount`
- **Webhook receiver** — mounted BEFORE `express.json()` using `express.raw()` for signature verification, HMAC-SHA256 signature check
- **BullMQ queue** — webhook events pushed to `githubQueue` → `githubWorker` processes
- **Events handled** — PR opened, PR merged, Push → creates Notification records + `emitToWorkspace`

### 9. Socket.io (Real-time)
- **Backend (`lib/socket.ts`):**
  - `initSocket(httpServer)` — called once at startup
  - **Auth middleware** — reads JWT from httpOnly cookie (`cookie.parse(socket.handshake.headers.cookie)`)
  - **Personal room** — `user:{userId}` (multi-device support)
  - **Workspace room** — `workspace:{workspaceId}` (auto-leave previous on switch)
  - **Member access check** — `join:workspace` verifies membership before joining room
  - `emitToUser(userId, event, data)` — personal notification
  - `emitToWorkspace(workspaceId, event, data)` — broadcast to workspace
  - `getIO()` — global access for services/webhooks
- **Frontend (`shared/lib/socket.ts`):**
  - Singleton pattern — `connectSocket()` creates-or-returns, `disconnectSocket()` tears down
  - `autoConnect: true`, `transports: ["websocket"]`, reconnection (5 attempts, 1s delay)
  - `WorkspaceLayout` — single place that calls `connectSocket()` + `socket.emit("join:workspace")` + registers RT listener

### 10. Notifications
- **DB storage** — `Notification` model, cursor-based pagination (limit 20)
- **`useNotifications`** — `useInfiniteQuery`, cursor pagination, "Load More" button
- **`useRTNotifications`** — socket `notification:new` listener, updates first page of infinite query cache via `queryClient.setQueryData<InfiniteData<NotificationResponse>>`
- **Unread count** — separate dedicated `useQuery` (`staleTime: Infinity`, `refetchOnWindowFocus: false`) — NOT derived from paginated list (accurate count regardless of pages loaded)
- **Mark all read** — `PATCH` API, updates only unread-count cache (not full list)
- **Bell icon** — in sidebar header (industry-standard placement), shows red badge with count (9+ capped)
- **Notifications page** — paginated list, unread items highlighted, timestamps

### 11. Activity Log
- **Workspace-level audit trail** — every major action recorded
- **Actions tracked** — WORKSPACE_UPDATED, PROJECT_CREATED/UPDATED/DELETED, ISSUE_CREATED/UPDATED/DELETED/STATUS_CHANGED/PRIORITY_CHANGED/ASSIGNED, MEMBER_JOINED/REMOVED/ROLE_CHANGED, PR_OPENED/MERGED/CLOSED, PUSH, etc.
- **Actor preserved in metadata** — even after member delete (SetNull on actorId, but name/details in metadata JSON)
- **Recent activities** — dashboard widget

### 12. User Profile
- **View profile** — `GET /api/users/:username`
- **Edit profile** — name, username, mobile, avatar (Cloudinary upload, old avatar deleted)
- **Change email** — OTP-based (OTP sent to new email, verified, then updated)
- **Change password** — OTP-based (authenticated flow)

### 13. Routing Architecture
- **`createBrowserRouter`** with `future: { v7_startTransition: true }` — fixes navigation freeze/blank-UI during lazy chunk download
- **Lazy loading** — all pages lazy via `React.lazy()` + per-route `<Suspense fallback={<MainLoder/>}>` via `withSuspense` helper; layouts eager
- **Guard pattern** — `AuthGuard` (blocks /auth for logged-in), `PrivateGuard` (blocks / for unauthenticated)
- **`WorkspaceLayout`** — validates slug against workspace list, redirects to `/` if invalid slug (with toast), persists valid slug to `localStorage`
- **`Redirect`** — smart redirect using `lastWorkspace` localStorage, falls back to first workspace, sets localStorage
- **Profile routes** — top-level (not workspace-scoped), accessible even with 0 workspaces

### 14. TanStack Query Architecture
- **Global defaults** — `staleTime: 60000`, `refetchOnWindowFocus: false` in `QueryClient` constructor
- **Per-hook overrides** — `staleTime: Infinity` for socket-driven data (notifications, unread count)
- **Deduplication** — same `queryKey` = single network request even if hook called from 4 components simultaneously
- **Cache invalidation** — `invalidateQueries` on mutations (create/update/delete)
- **Optimistic updates** — notification cache updated immediately on socket event (no refetch needed)
- **Infinite query** — notifications use `useInfiniteQuery` with cursor-based pagination

### 15. Error Handling
- **`AppError`** — custom class with `statusCode`
- **Global `errorMiddleware`** — handles `AppError`, `ZodError`, `PrismaClientKnownRequestError` (P2002 duplicate with field-specific messages, P2025 not found)
- **Frontend `setFormErrors`** — bridges axios errors + Zod errors into React Hook Form `setError`
- **Axios interceptor** — 401 → queue requests → refresh token → retry; if refresh fails → logout

---

## Key Architectural Decisions

| Decision | Choice | Reason |
|----------|--------|--------|
| OTP storage | Redis (not DB) | Temporary data, TTL auto-expire, no cleanup needed |
| OTP security | bcrypt hash | Plain text OTP never stored |
| Socket auth | httpOnly cookie | Token not accessible via JS, more secure |
| Notification unread count | Separate query | Paginated list gives inaccurate count |
| `socket.to()` vs `io.to()` | `io.to()` everywhere | No client-initiated broadcasts in current scope |
| Invite token storage | URL query param | Persists across tab close/refresh, no cleanup needed |
| Profile routes | Top-level (not workspace-scoped) | User can have 0 workspaces |
| Form pattern | `mutateAsync` (not `mutate`) | RHF `isSubmitting` tracks correctly |
| Permission check | Frontend UI hide + Backend middleware | Defense in depth |
| `Activity.actorId` | `onDelete: SetNull` | Preserve audit history even after member removal |

